From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Screensaver: build a title sequence in the background and
 take it in

screensaver.build(sequence) runs the generator that its installer named in
<user directory>/screensaver/generator.json (a Python interpreter and a
script called mksequence.py) for that title sequence, in the background and
without a console window, its output in <user directory>/screensaver/build.log.
A plugin passes only the sequence's name, so it cannot choose what runs.
screensaver.buildStatus reports the build (idle, running, done, failed,
cancelled) and cancelBuild() stops it.

The generator writes the new sequence to
<user directory>/screensaver/build/live/<name>. screensaver.applyBuild(name)
copies it into the installed title sequence of that name, which must be the
one playing and a folder (new files written beside their place and renamed
over it, parks the new script no longer names removed), and reloads the
playing sequence's script: the park on screen keeps playing, and the
plugin's next seek loads from the new script, in the background as before.
ITitleSequencePlayer gains Reload() for that.
